    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-31T21:18:32+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-31T21:18:32+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T11:48:32Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T11:48:32Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred over eastern NSW extends a ridge over SA. The ridge will weaken and the high will move eastwards on Tuesday and a cold front is expected to move across SA. Another high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and another cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough and cold front will move over SA during the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW007" description="Murraylands" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-31T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Light winds.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. High chance of showers, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the southwest in the afternoon and evening. Winds northerly 15 to 25 km/h increasing to 25 to 40 km/h in the morning then turning westerly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 2:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Light winds becoming westerly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds westerly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Winds northerly and light increasing to 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then turning northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 6 with daytime temperatures reaching around 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
